<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
  L2 run settings, applied automatically: Directory.Build.props points Dlo.Game.Tests at this
  file via RunSettingsFilePath, so `dotnet test` needs no extra flag and the invocation in the
  README stays one command.

  Parameters below are appended to the Godot process GdUnit4 launches to RUN tests. Its
  separate compile pass already runs headless; the test-runner pass does not, and on a CI
  runner with no display that kills the process and surfaces as a connection timeout.
  Observed on ubuntu-latest, 2026-08-24. The README's "Three L2 gotchas" section has the
  full account, including why the error message points at the wrong thing.

  Applied everywhere and not only in CI, deliberately: local and CI running the same command
  with different arguments is how a suite goes green on the machine nobody works on.
-->

<RunSettings>
  <GdUnit4>
    <Parameters>--headless</Parameters>
  </GdUnit4>
</RunSettings>
